  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ FRAL-Empowering Women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s main goal is to promote and improve women&apos;s living standards through entrepreneurship, business, and technical skillsin order to diversify their livelihood opportunities and reduce poverty. This project&apos;s anticipated changes include: 1) increased access to control and ownership of livelihood assets to increase opportunities for women to acquire, use, add value to, and profit from livelihood assets and investments. 2) Enabling women&apos;s financial inclusion, market access, and value chain participation. 3) Improved business and entrepreneurship skills to increase women&apos;s (rights holders&apos;) capacity to establish and manage long-term economic activities. 4) Enhanced women&apos;s leadership and accountability skills, as well as created a space for political participation. To that end, the project will train groups in economic rights and core life skills such as leadership, teamwork, and effective communication, as well as business planning, networking, and marketing. connecting the groups with relevantstakeholders to gain access to technical and mentoring support tailored to their specific enterprise The project will assist all groups in obtaining the necessary financial capital as well as financial literacy training, as well as in establishing savingsgroups and establishing links with financial institutions. The project will advocate for economic justice and respond to local government decision makers in order to create an enabling environment for women to expand their businesses and take advantage ofother economic opportunities, such as equal opportunities, markets, innovation, technology, and ownership of economic assets/resources. In this case, FRAL will persuade women to conduct a community power analysis in order to address all forms of power imbalances that lead to the deprivation of women&apos;s economic rights, including the right to own property and productive resources such as land.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FONDATION FOR RESEARCH AND ASSISTAN</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foundation for Research and Assistance in Law (FRAL) is a nonprofit,
non-governmental organization founded in early 2012 but the official
registration happened on the 23rd day of June, 2014. The aim of the
organization is to promote human rights, gender equality and access
to justice to vulnerable women, youth and children. The founder
members saw that although there were various ongoing interventions
both by the public sector and the civil society on provision of legal aid,
but still there was a significant scarcity of free legal assistance and
legal education to the needy. As a result, the founders decided to
establish this organization so as to contribute to those pre-existing
efforts in promoting access to justice. The goal of our organization is to promote human rights, gender equality and access to justice to vulnerable women, youth, people with disabilities and children FRAL vision is a Tanzania where the marginalized community have no injustice and inequality in all aspect of life.FRAL&#x2019;s core values include excellence, ccreativity,innovativeness, integrity, accountability, partnerships, transparency, responsibility, respect for others and networking</narrative>
  </participating-org>
